		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T16:46:08Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Expand trusted paths and add executable magic-number detection\n\nSubmodule sync bringing three complementary improvements for extension runtime reliability:\n\n1. **Extended trusted paths** (`PathSecurity.rs`):\n   - Add `/tmp`, `/private/tmp`, `/var/tmp` for language servers (ruby-lsp, pyright, etc.)\n   - Add third-party tool state: `~/.gitkraken`, `~/.gk`, `~/.copilot`, `~/.config/git`\n   - Add read-only POSIX OS files (`/etc/os-release`, `/proc/*`, etc.)\n\n2. **Magic-number executable detection** (`VsixInstaller.rs`):\n   - Probe file headers for ELF, Mach-O fat/thin, and shebang\n   - Detect bin paths (`bin/`, `server/`, `tools/`, `omnisharp`, `adapter`, `native`)\n   - Promote 0o644 → 0o755 for detected executables, fixing EACCES on spawn\n   - Add `HealExecutableBits()` to retroactively fix pre-existing installs\n\n3. **Boot-time exec-bit heal** (`Scanner.rs`):\n   - Walk user extensions (`~/.land/extensions/`) at scan time\n   - Apply same heuristic to recover extensions installed before the fix\n\n4. **Benign ENOENT** (`DevLog.rs`): Add vim registers, globalStorage probing, chat editing sessions.\n\nImpact: Extension binaries (rust-analyzer, GitLens, Copilot) that were failing with EACCES due to missing exec bits now run correctly.",
			"SHA": "991e3b34886434902061a9b60f74bf790222c473"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T15:37:49Z",
			"File": [
				"⡇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Add land-native search provider and expose ISearchService\n\nCross-cutting search integration across Sky, Output, and Mountain:\n\n- **Sky (b4358aa9):** Add search result provider routing VS Code's Search viewlet queries through Mountain's `search:findFiles` / `search:findInFiles` handlers. The stock web's `RemoteSearchService` relies on File System Access API which returns `undefined` for Mountain-based filesystem, causing silent zero-result returns. New provider registers for both `file` (0) and `text` (1) search types, translating Mountain hits into `IFileMatch` shape. Also add global exception cap to PostHogBridge to prevent CDN limit flooding (configurable via `LAND_POSTHOG_SKY_EXCEPTION_GLOBAL_LIMIT`, defaults to 7).\n\n- **Output (f651b48f):** Extend ExposeWorkbenchAccessor ESBuild transform to expose ISearchService alongside existing Statusbar, Commands, and CommandRegistry services. Adds require for `vs/workbench/services/search/common/search` and includes `Search` entry in `__CEL_SERVICES__` global, enabling Sky-side bridge code to access search service without re-entering AMD loader.\n\n- **Cocoon (5bc55a9f):** Submodule sync.\n\nImpact: Search functionality now works in the Land editor with Mountain-based filesystem. PostHog exception telemetry respects CDN rate limits.",
			"SHA": "b0c61117bc38976c071b8690baa6017a75eec5c4"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T15:08:08Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add trusted system paths bypass and idempotent VSIX installs\n\nUpdate Mountain submodule with two related extension-management improvements:\n1. **Trusted system paths** (`PathSecurity.rs`): Add `IsTrustedSystemPath` that defines directories Land owns (`.land/`, Application Support, bundled extension roots, TMPDIR) which bypass the workspace-folder sandbox check. Enables the extension scanner to read `~/.land/extensions` for user-installed VSIXes.\n2. **Idempotent VSIX reinstalls** (`VsixInstaller.rs`): Remove `AlreadyInstalled` error and treat re-installs as no-op when target already exists with a readable manifest. Matches VS Code semantics and prevents renderer crash from null result dereference. Corrupt/partial installs are wiped and re-extracted.\n\nBoth changes unblock the extension loading pipeline, allowing user-installed extensions to appear in the Extensions sidebar.",
			"SHA": "dffce14837d3c5824a7fff68ae59a46f40915955"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T14:49:36Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠁⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				6
			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Wire status bar and command bridges, enhance dev diagnostics\n\nCross-cutting integration across Output, Sky, and Mountain submodules:\n\n- **Output (354c448c):** Enhance ExposeWorkbenchAccessor transform to pre-resolve concrete service instances (IStatusbarService, ICommandService, CommandRegistry) into globalThis.__CEL_SERVICES__ during workbench startup. Allows Sky-side bridge code to call methods directly without re-entering the AMD loader.\n\n- **Sky (ea2932ae):** Wire status bar and command bridges into workbench services. Extension-contributed status bar items (from `vscode.window.createStatusBarItem()`) now route through `IStatusbarService.addEntry()`. Add command bridge layer: `sky://command/execute` invokes `ICommandService.executeCommand`, `sky://command/register` registers into CommandsRegistry with fan-out back to Cocoon, `sky://command/unregister` disposes.\n\n- **Mountain (f1de83d5):** Add payload preview (160 bytes max) to notification-drop logging for diagnostic clarity. Register benign ENOENT paths: MCP config files, user snippets/keybindings, AI workspace storage, git config for non-repos.\n\n- **Common + Maintain:** Dependency bumps for pozil/auto-assign-issue (2.2.0→3.0.0) and @cloudflare/workers-types.\n\nImpact: Extension status bar items now render in native VS Code DOM. Extension commands execute against the workbench with proper bidirectional binding.",
			"SHA": "c8d8c6d920b73f5f434c53c659ab2ebb01f4ed74"
		}
	],
